# Git workflow

Never develop directly on `main`. This clone may have **no remote** — do not create a GitHub repo unless the human names the owner.

Long-lived: `main` (protected) ← `develop` ← work branches.

Work branches: `feature/*`, `fix/*` (aliases `bugfix/`, `feat/`), `refactor/*`, `experiment/*`, plus `docs/`, `test/`, `chore/`. Integration branch: **`develop`** (not `development` until an ADR).

One agent-owned feature branch at a time; do not blindly co-edit.

Substantial work: branch → implement → tests → diff → review → PR → CI → **human approval** → merge. Quality gates: `docs/QUALITY_GATES.md`.

AI must not: merge to `main`, merge PRs, delete branches/repos, force-push, or `git reset --hard` of shared history.

Do not commit `.env`, keys, or model weights. Conventional Commits are required.
